{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Behold, a place is with Me.</b> On the mountain where I speak with you always, there is a place ready for Me for your need — that I may hide you there so that you not be harmed, and from there you will see what you will see; this is its plain sense. And its midrash: concerning a place where the Shechinah speaks, and it says 'the place is with Me' — and it does not say 'I am in the place,' for the Holy One, blessed be He, is the place of the world, and the world is not His place (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:24.618460947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}